{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T17:47:46.914Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f77002cf3a055dd016a9ee063f4e087d2aef9902fc70e02a5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_TGISnvlTOcAD6UvOdf7aIYaQ","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\\n@@\\n-- ambiguous loose-file dependency imports expose an opaque `dependencySelectionRevision` with their advertised candidates. Guided retries must echo that revision together with `dependencySourcePackageIds`; any intervening workspace-file mutation returns a failed import with `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale`, requiring a fresh candidate review before immutable assembly\\n+- ambiguous loose-file dependency imports expose an opaque `dependencySelectionRevision` with their advertised candidates. Guided retries must echo that revision together with `dependencySourcePackageIds`; any intervening workspace-file mutation returns a failed import with `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale`, requiring a fresh candidate review before immutable assembly. The final automatic or manually reviewed ZIP plus its lineage event are reserved atomically against that same complete workspace revision in every store, so a concurrent upload, replacement, deletion, or competing assembly cannot commit a stale or duplicate dependency snapshot\\n@@\\n-- loose source-package intake resolves unique original `Booklet` or `SysCheck` → `Unit` → Verona player, `DefinitionRef`, `VariablesRef`, coding-scheme, and separately uploaded `.itcr.zip` player-resource references across already uploaded workspace files. Starting the root import captures that transitive closure in a new immutable dependency-snapshot ZIP, records exact member lineage, selects the snapshot in Angular, and runs the normal importer; the original resource-package gate proves the resulting participant download in memory, file, and SQLite stores. Ambiguous references produce structured diagnostics with one Angular action per exact candidate. The chosen source-package ID is validated server-side, retained across later ambiguity decisions, and captured with the remaining unique dependency closure in the same audited immutable snapshot; incomplete matches still fail explicitly. The sequential loose-file queue exposes its processed count, exact current file, accessible determinate progress, and workspace-refresh phase while disabling duplicate submission; successful files enter reviewed assembly immediately and the final best-effort report remains itemized. Manual assembly remains as the controlled fallback for deliberate 2–100-file composition, rejecting missing documents, unsafe relative paths, duplicate selection ids, case-insensitive duplicate archive paths, and per-file/aggregate size overflow while preserving an existing manifest or generating compatible IMS aliases from paths, original XML metadata, and Verona JSON-LD module identity/version metadata\\n+- loose source-package intake resolves unique original `Booklet` or `SysCheck` → `Unit` → Verona player, `DefinitionRef`, `VariablesRef`, coding-scheme, and separately uploaded `.itcr.zip` player-resource references across already uploaded workspace files. Starting the root import captures that transitive closure in a new immutable dependency-snapshot ZIP, records exact member lineage, selects the snapshot in Angular, and runs the normal importer; the original resource-package gate proves the resulting participant download in memory, file, and SQLite stores. Ambiguous references produce structured diagnostics with one Angular action per exact candidate. The chosen source-package ID is validated server-side, retained across later ambiguity decisions, and captured with the remaining unique dependency closure in the same audited immutable snapshot; incomplete matches still fail explicitly. Snapshot package and assembly evidence are committed together only if the complete source-package/activity revision still matches; otherwise the import or manual assembly returns a retryable conflict without leaving a partial aggregate. The sequential loose-file queue exposes its processed count, exact current file, accessible determinate progress, and workspace-refresh phase while disabling duplicate submission; successful files enter reviewed assembly immediately and the final best-effort report remains itemized. Manual assembly remains as the controlled fallback for deliberate 2–100-file composition, rejecting missing documents, unsafe relative paths, duplicate selection ids, case-insensitive duplicate archive paths, and per-file/aggregate size overflow while preserving an existing manifest or generating compatible IMS aliases from paths, original XML metadata, and Verona JSON-LD module identity/version metadata\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n-| 4 | P1 | Workspace batch edge cases | Add broader replacement graphs and concurrent dependency changes in replacement/import workflows outside the guided candidate-selection path. Guided ambiguity diagnostics carry an opaque revision of the exact workspace file population shown to the operator; every selected retry must echo it, and any intervening replacement/upload/delete fails closed as `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale` until the ambiguity is refreshed. Memory/file/SQLite API coverage mutates a two-candidate relationship into three candidates between review and mutation, and production Chromium proves the stale warning, refresh, revised request, and successful immutable snapshot. Source deletion now closes its separate request-time race as well: the application hashes every dependency-relevant file state and assembly/replacement edge used for readiness, all stores compare that revision atomically with import/release guards, and PostgreSQL serializes reference mutations on the workspace row. Store tests cover both a newly added root and an in-place root-document change; the existing durable API matrix retains request-order-independent multi-level deletion with failed-root retention. Replacement lineage also distinguishes retained audit history from live successors: deleting a rejected replacement and its failed import cannot leave the valid predecessor falsely superseded. A three-generation rollback now proves that deleting a live chain tip reopens only its direct predecessor for another replacement while the original remains superseded by its still-live child across every durable API store. Broader replacement-lineage behavior remains. |\\n+| 4 | P1 | Workspace batch edge cases | Add broader replacement graphs outside the now-guarded import/assembly paths. Guided ambiguity diagnostics carry an opaque revision of the exact workspace file population shown to the operator; every selected retry must echo it, and any intervening replacement/upload/delete fails closed as `source_document_workspace_dependency_selection_stale` until the ambiguity is refreshed. The final automatic dependency snapshot and manually reviewed assembly now reserve their source package plus lineage event atomically against the complete source-package/activity revision in memory, file, SQLite, and PostgreSQL. A concurrent upload, replacement, deletion, or second assembly therefore returns a retryable conflict without a partial aggregate; store races prove exactly one package/event pair can win a revision. Source deletion closes its separate request-time race as well: the application hashes every dependency-relevant file state and assembly/replacement edge used for readiness, all stores compare that revision atomically with import/release guards, and PostgreSQL serializes reference mutations on the workspace row. Store tests cover both a newly added root and an in-place root-document change; the existing durable API matrix retains request-order-independent multi-level deletion with failed-root retention. Replacement lineage also distinguishes retained audit history from live successors: deleting a rejected replacement and its failed import cannot leave the valid predecessor falsely superseded. A three-generation rollback proves that deleting a live chain tip reopens only its direct predecessor for another replacement while the original remains superseded by its still-live child across every durable API store. Broader replacement-lineage behavior remains. |\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07c91-ea1b-7230-b7b6-d6992ec2e7dd","create_time":1788797022.360362}}}
