{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T17:47:46.931Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07cab-1c85-79c3-884d-83c9882fdbc9","call_id":"call_OabqdIlVZ7rcbhvlbBYMMri7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e79583\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003958,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1228,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\nentire session — Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\\nView and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\\n\\nCommands:\\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\\n\\nExamples:\\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\\n\\nCurrent repo: gh/jurei733/testcenter-rewrite  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\\n\\nInherited flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\\nSubcommands: adopt · attach · current · info · list · resume · stop · tokens\\n             read-only except: adopt, attach, resume, stop\\nNext:  entire agent-help session <subcommand>\\nView and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\\n\\nCommands:\\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\\n\\nExamples:\\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire session [command]\\n\\nAliases:\\n  session, sessions\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  adopt       Adopt an active session from another worktree\\n  attach      Attach an existing agent session\\n  current     Show the active session for the current worktree\\n  info        Show detailed session information\\n  list        List all sessions\\n  resume      Resume a stopped session (interactive picker, or by branch)\\n  stop        Stop one or more active sessions\\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a session\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for session\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\\nUse \\\"entire session [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"019ff816-9f64-7f83-8a27-cb7801f6d990\\\",\\n    \\\"agent\\\": \\\"Codex\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"ended\\\",\\n    \\\"started_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-06T21:43:02.411744+02:00\\\",\\n    \\\"last_active\\\": \\\"2026-09-06T21:43:02.411744+02:00\\\",\\n    \\\"turns\\\": 134,\\n    \\\"checkpoints\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"last_checkpoint_id\\\": \\\"01M1W3X3RVDCK2XC818BZY6R9Y\\\",\\n    \\\"tokens\\\": {\\n      \\\"total\\\": 1720546631,\\n      \\\"input\\\": 38603701,\\n      \\\"cache_read\\\": 1678768128,\\n      \\\"cache_write\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"output\\\": 3174802\\n    },\\n    \\\"last_prompt\\\": \\\"Arbeite im Repo /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app autonom weiter.\\\\n\\\\nZiel: Testcenter-Rewrite als lauffähige, produktionsnahe Anwendung mit möglichst hoher Parität zum ursprünglichen Testcenter fertigstellen.\\\\n\\\\nLies zuerst docs/PARITY.md, README.md, git status und die letzten 15 Commits.\\\\nSetze anschließend immer den nächsten sinnvollsten Implementierungsschritt um.\\\\n\\\\nAktueller nächster Kandidat:\\\\nPrüfe und implementiere den teilnehmerisolierten Review-CSV-Download auf der Participant-Starterseite entsprechend dem Original-Ablauf „Reviews downloaden“. Review-Erfassung und Admin-Export existieren bereits.\\\\n\\\\nBewahre die ungetrackte Datei docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx unverändert.\\\\nCommitte sinnvolle abgeschlossene Schritte. Nicht pushen, bis ich darum bitte.\\\\nFrage nicht nach „weiter?“.\\\"\\n  }\\n]\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07c91-ea1b-7230-b7b6-d6992ec2e7dd","create_time":1788797983.877091}}}
